  "notation": "Adm 1002.08",
  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/adm1000.html",
  "prefLabel": "Adm 1002.08 Minimum liability for legal expenses",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Adm 1002.08 \"Minimum liability for legal expenses\" means the sum of money ordered by the presiding judge to be repaid the state by a defendant for whom counsel has been appointed, exclusive of any additional liability incurred as a result of orders for state payment of defense services other than counsel and for state payment of expenses.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Adm 1000) #8697, eff 8-3-06; ss by #9149, eff 5-1-08 (from Adm 1002.05); ss by #10728, eff 11-25-14; ss by #13050, eff 7-1-20 (formerly Adm 1002.06)",
